# [TNG Crews](tng_crews)

The senior staff of the four ships everyone already knows, bound to the hulls that wear
their silhouettes. Sit at engineering on a Galaxy-class and you are Geordi.

`Hull:` is the MOD tier of the crew resolution - it says "any ship of this class arrives
with these people" and loses to a mission naming its own crew for a named ship, to an
operator picking a roster for the game, and to anything a player chose about themselves.
So this is an answer, never an imposition.

Each member carries a `Portrait:`, not a `Face:`. The 127 portraits register out of the
media pack with nothing to install; the 568 face cells need `data/graphics/allFaceFiles.txt`
edited by hand, which a mastlib cannot do, so a face here would silently fail to draw for
most installs.

No `Gender:` anywhere here, deliberately. That field says which face to ROLL for somebody
who has none of their own, and everyone below carries a portrait; the faces behind them are
a mod race's whole drawn busts, which have no gender axis to steer. The stock crews use it
because a terran face is built from parts and does have one.

Hulls with no cast - Sovereign, Akira, Nebula, Luna and the rest - are deliberately absent.
They are nobody's ship, so they get an automatic crew like any other, and every one of them
is a different person.

## [Enterprise-D](tng_enterprise_d)
